# Virtual environment
.venv/
venv/
ENV/

# Python caching
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# User configurations (private keys & tokens)
config/api_keys.json
config/google_token.json
config/certs/*.key
config/certs/*.crt


# Local databases and runtime state.
#
# Every file in memory/ that is not code is the user's private life: names of
# family and partners, habits, projects. install.sh git-clones into
# ~/.aethelark, so every installation is a git checkout and anything not
# ignored here is one `git add -A` away from being published. Naming
# long_term.json alone was not enough - memory_manager.py writes a sibling
# long_term.bak on every save, and that .bak reached the public repo with real
# personal data in it.
#
# So: ignore the whole directory and re-admit the code explicitly. A new
# runtime file cannot leak by being forgotten; it has to be allow-listed.
memory/*
!memory/*.py
memory/__pycache__/

# Whatever the user drops into the dashboard. dashboard/server.py creates
# BASE_DIR/uploads at runtime, so these are their files, in a git checkout,
# for the same reason memory/ was.
uploads/
dashboard/__pycache__/
config/__pycache__/
actions/__pycache__/

# IDEs & System files
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
scratch/

# Secrets — OAuth tokens & TLS keys (must never be committed)
config/google_token.json
config/certs/*.key
config/certs/*.crt

# debug screenshots
screenshot_*.png
